; Generated from packaging/uninstall-associations.nsh.in - edit that, not this.
;
; Removes what install-associations.nsh registered.
;
; Note what is *not* removed: HKCU\Software\TopicDev\Makimedia, where the
; settings live, nor the library database under AppData. Reinstalling and
; finding the whole library gone is worse than leaving a few values behind.

@MM_NSIS_DELETE_PROGIDS@

DeleteRegKey HKCU "Software\Classes\Makimedia.Video"
DeleteRegKey HKCU "Software\Classes\Applications\@MM_EXECUTABLE_NAME@"

System::Call 'shell32::SHChangeNotify(i 0x08000000, i 0, i 0, i 0)'
